<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wars in Lombardy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1423">1423</a>–<a href="/years/1454">1454</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Wars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> were a series of conflicts from 1423 to 1454 between the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> and other Italian states drawn in. Fought largely by condottieri such as Carmagnola, Gattamelata and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-sforza">Francesco Sforza</a>, they extended Venice's mainland territory to the Adda and ended with the Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi</a> (1454), which brought a balance of power to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wars-in-lombardy.jpg" alt="Wars in Lombardy" width="320" height="233" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Paul Rubens / After Leonardo da Vinci · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Paul_Ruben%27s_copy_of_the_lost_Battle_of_Anghiari.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
